<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhenzhu Khagan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 645</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Yinan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhenzhu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">Khagan</a>, personal name Yinan, was the leader of the Xueyantuo, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiele">Tiele</a> people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. He led their revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-turkic-khaganate">Eastern Turkic Khaganate</a> in 628 and was recognised as khagan by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Emperor Taizong of Tang</a>. After the Turks fell in 630 he made the Xueyantuo the dominant power in the steppe, but relations with the Tang soured and his state collapsed soon after his death in 645.</p></div>
